    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T15:56:56Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/1805-exact-side-carry · PR #1932 · pinned by a_contoured_wall_keeps_its_off_grid_position_after_a_side_turn, a_pocket_remains_cut_after_a_side_turn_and_return, a_fixture_touching_the_turned_machined_wall_is_contact · merges when reviewed\n\nBox stock with retained cut history preserves machined walls and cavities through side turns.\nAll 40 targeted tests pass. All 18 mutations fail, then pass after restoration.\nThe quick gate and clippy pass.\n\nThe field engine keeps FIELD_SIDE_CARRY_REFUSAL.\nIts vertical cut records cannot prove material intervals along a new axis.\nRe-indexing its bricks alone cannot make that read safe.\nMesh stock, cylinder stock, and grids without retained history keep the existing conservative carry.\n",
